TRACED (v9.3, confidence HIGH): Front wheel-speed scaling divisor: sets distance per front ABS pulse, so it carries front tire rolling circumference and the tone-ring tooth count. FUN_76F44 forms front raw wheel speed fef02634 = (front pulse fef027a8 x 57600 / this) / timebase << 2, output X/128 km/h. A taller or larger-circumference front tire covers more ground per pulse and makes the ECM read low, so LOWER this to correct it: new = round(48 x stock_circumference / new_circumference). Stock 48; 8-bit, so each count is about 2 percent (coarse). Also read by the front-speed check FUN_77568. Changing it moves the speedometer and the front wheel speed used by traction control, anti-lift, launch and cruise.
