TRACED (v9.3, confidence HIGH): Rear wheel-speed scaling divisor, main term: with the fine term 0x18EFD8 it sets distance per rear ABS pulse, carrying rear tire rolling circumference and the tone-ring tooth count. FUN_770A8 forms rear raw wheel speed fef02636 = (rear pulse fef0262e x 57600 / (this x 0x18EFD8) << 8) / timebase, output X/128 km/h; the same pair feeds the rear-speed / odometer paths FUN_5627E, FUN_56310 and FUN_563A8. A taller or larger-circumference rear tire makes the ECM read low, so LOWER the effective divisor to correct it: new product (this x 0x18EFD8) = round(3200 x stock_circumference / new_circumference). Change this 8-bit term (stock 50, ~2 percent per count) for coarse steps or 0x18EFD8 for fine. Feeds the speedometer and the rear wheel speed used by traction control, wheelie control and gear-ratio detection.
